          <Pad Id="RrBWk2XaB3LbnPuR7ddE55" Comment="the path as WKT - each edge keeps its own geometry" Bounds="60,930,900,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Pad Id="RYblZueqeHHmA4XsBgEiDb" Bounds="60,980,900,250" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Connectivity is exact shared endpoints: no tolerance, no automatic noding. Two lines that cross without sharing an endpoint are not connected, and an interior vertex is shape, not a junction. Shorten the diagonal to LINESTRING (0 0, 2 2) and it dangles: the path goes round the square, 8 instead of 5.66. Point To at 11 10 and Found turns False with an empty path - the island shares no endpoint with the square. Max Snap Distance (default: infinite) refuses a From or To that lies further than that from any node, and reports the refusal the same way.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Out of scope on purpose, and not a promise for later: one-way streets, turn costs, speeds and travel time, A*, nearest-point-on-edge snapping, OSM import. The scope is one sentence - an undirected network of explicitly connected LineStrings in a local Cartesian space, with length as cost, Dijkstra as the algorithm.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation>
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
